    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0325" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg67"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2245</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Droppers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-13T12:00:00+01:34">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 13, 1915, 12 noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. Germany and Bulgaria have raised the question of what the Greek Government as
                    a neutral proposed to do with regard to the Servians, English, and French in
                    case they were driven back into <pb facs="0326" n="68" xml:id="pg68"/> Greek
                    territory. French Minister informed the new Prime Minister Skouloudis that if a
                    single soldier of the Allies was disarmed by Greek authority the consequences
                    would be grave. Situation acute.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Droppers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
